<article class="env-definition" id="01NF">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/01NF">Definition <span data-tag="01NF">27.13.2</span>.</a> The scheme $\mathbf{P}^ n_{\mathbf{Z}} = \text{Proj}(\mathbf{Z}[T_0, \ldots , T_ n])$ is called <em>projective $n$-space over $\mathbf{Z}$</em>. Its base change $\mathbf{P}^ n_ S$ to a scheme $S$ is called <em>projective $n$-space over $S$</em>. If $R$ is a ring the base change to $\mathop{\mathrm{Spec}}(R)$ is denoted $\mathbf{P}^ n_ R$ and called <em>projective $n$-space over $R$</em>. </p>
</article>